  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Amend ADR-027 §3 (concise + full): managed default for customer environments, unmanaged on explicit instruction (`solutionPackageType`, recorded on the registry row), dev unmanaged, one solution SpaarkeMaster; drop "do not enforce managed".</step>
    <step order="2">Rewrite SPAARKE-SOLUTION-RELEASE-PROCESS.md as "Spaarke solution package — release, IAM and upgrade runbook": scope rule + exclusions, git source of record, release steps, first import (H6), upgrade (StageAndUpgrade; removals delete components; values persist; downgrade and type switch refused; H6 before H9), IAM (importing identity = System Administrator via H10; roles ship in the package).</step>
    <step order="3">Correct production-release.md, ci-cd-workflow.md, the deployment guide H6 row + the 8-solution passage, and the inventory rows to point at the runbook (one solution, managed by default).</step>
    <step order="4">Grep for remaining "9 solutions"/"8 solutions"/"unmanaged everywhere" claims in docs/ and .claude/; fix or list them; commit.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Both ADR-027 files state managed-by-default + unmanaged-on-explicit-instruction; neither says "unmanaged everywhere" as current practice.</criterion>
